<title>UK: Bank of Ireland sets 150 mln stg 12-yr step-up FRN.</title>
<headline>Bank of Ireland sets 150 mln stg 12-yr step-up FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated floating-rate issue was announced by joint lead managers J.P. Morgan, Lehman Brothers and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANK OF IRELAND</p>
<p> AMT    150 MLN STG   SPREAD     *+35 BP   MATURITY   *11.FEB.09</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 BASE	 3M LIBOR  PAY DATE    11.FEB.97</p>
<p> EXP MOODY  A2	  ISS PRICE  99.90     FULL FEES   0.40</p>
<p> EXP S&amp;P    A-</p>
<p> NOTES	*FOR FIRST SEVEN YEARS, THEN +85 BP IF NOT CALLED</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 100	 SALE LIMITS US/UK/IE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 1</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC  0.20	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
